# No .dockerignore existed before this (found live, D54 verification-walk
# session: three successive `docker compose build [--no-cache] nginx`
# attempts served a byte-identical bundle despite confirmed source changes
# and a genuinely freshly-recreated container -- this file was the missing
# piece, alongside a suspected stale Windows/WSL2 filesystem-bridge view of
# the build context; see claude/progress-ledger.md).
#
# Without this, Dockerfile.nginx's `COPY . .` (which runs AFTER `RUN npm ci`)
# drags the host's own node_modules, dist/, and .git into the build context
# and OVERWRITES the container's just-installed, linux-correct node_modules
# with the host's Windows-native one -- including esbuild's platform binary,
# which the Dockerfile explicitly strips one line earlier
# (`rm -rf node_modules/.vite node_modules/esbuild`) for exactly this reason,
# but had nothing stopping it from coming right back via the unrestricted
# COPY. It also means every build ships hundreds of MB of irrelevant host
# state through the build context for no reason.
node_modules
dist
.git
.storybook
storybook-static
coverage
*.log
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.vscode
